                <pb facs="0122" n="114" xml:id="pg114"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94 Conference/122: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-10-28T10:00:00+00:00">October 28, 1937—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 28—8:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1533. Following from Davis: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Department’s 3, October 23, 3 p.m.<anchor n="30" xml:id="d125-f1"/> last
                            clause. I shall of course be glad to confer with the Belgian Government
                            regarding possible agenda but it seems to me important to adhere to and
                            cultivate the view that while we desire and expect to cooperate with the
                            other powers concerned, other powers initiated and fostered the idea of
                            holding the Conference in furtherance of responsibility of planning, and
                            leadership should rest with them, our function being to collaborate. I
                            therefore purpose to proceed to Brussels this evening to pay appropriate
                            calls and exchange general views and suggestions with Belgian officials
                            and then probably withdraw and remain away from Brussels until
                            representatives of several other powers shall have arrived there.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
